# Base URL of the FastAPI backend.
#
# Leave unset to use the Vite dev-server proxy (/api -> http://127.0.0.1:8000).
# Set it to call a backend directly, e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8000/api
#
# This is a BUILD-TIME value. Vite inlines `import.meta.env.*` into the bundle, so
# changing it requires a rebuild, not a restart - and there is no way to change it
# in a running deployment. On Vercel, set it in Project Settings -> Environment
# Variables, in the environment that builds Production, and redeploy.
#
# The `/api` suffix is required and is not added for you: the client concatenates
# this with a path that already starts with a slash, so the base has to carry the
# prefix that the backend serves (app/config.py `api_prefix`).
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
#
# The Vite dev server reads a different variable, VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET, and takes it
# from the shell rather than from this file. See vite.config.js.
#
# A note on the same-origin default: the compose deployment serves the SPA and the API
# from one origin via nginx, which is why the default needs no value there. Vercel and
# Render are two origins, so this becomes required, and the backend's CORS_ORIGINS
# has to list the Vercel origin in response. Both directions are asserted by
# backend/tests/test_split_deployment_contract.py.
